    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>
thresh is a powerful 75 MB native binary that provisions WSL2 Linux environments from declarative YAML blueprints.

Features:
- Native AOT compilation (75 MB, zero dependencies)
- Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration for AI editors (VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf)
- Cross-platform container support (WSL2, containerd/nerdctl)
- GitHub Copilot SDK integration
- WSL2 integration for environment provisioning
- 12 built-in Linux distributions (Ubuntu, Alpine, Debian, Fedora, Rocky)
- AI-powered blueprint generation (OpenAI GPT-4o-mini, GitHub Copilot)
- Blueprint-based environment configuration
- Custom distribution support
- Interactive AI chat mode
- Real-time metrics and monitoring

Requirements:
- Windows 11 with WSL2 enabled
- .NET runtime NOT required (self-contained Native AOT binary)
    </description>
    <summary>Fast, native WSL2 environment provisioning with AI-powered blueprints and MCP integration</summary>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/dealer426/thresh/releases/tag/v1.5.0</releaseNotes>
    <tags>wsl wsl2 linux provisioning devops containers infrastructure ai blueprints dotnet native-aot cli</tags>
